==English==

===Etymology===
{{compound|en|short|stop}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|baseball}} The [[infield]] defensive [[player]] that stands between the [[second baseman]] and the [[third baseman]].
#: ''The '''shortstop''' ranged deep into the hole to make the stop.''
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} A nimble defender.
#: ''I'll play '''shortstop''' when we make our proposal.''
# {{lb|en|gambling}} A [[player]] who is short of money.
#* '''1981''', Sam Grafstein, ''Dice Doctor''
#*: The '''shortstops''' and desperados were not permitted to play in this marker crap game.

